In data science, the boundary between research and education is increasingly porous. 
Research drives methodological innovation and discovery, while education develops the skills, judgment, 
and habits of mind required to sustain that innovation. When intentionally integrated, research and education 
can form a mutually reinforcing system that accelerates discovery while producing more capable and adaptive learners.
